# S12-T03: Emit presence.sync on Join / Leave / Room-Change

## App-agent preflight

- [ ] `explain("work-control")` — realtime section
- [ ] Confirm T02 DONE: `presence.ts` registry exists

## Implementation

Extend `server/routes/_ws.ts`:

```ts
// On open: peer starts with no rooms — no broadcast yet
// On subscribe (message handler): when rooms change
//   1. leaveRoom(oldRoom, peerId) for removed rooms
//   2. joinRoom(newRoom, { id: peerId, kind: 'human', label: 'User …' }) for added rooms
//   3. broadcast presence.sync to all affected rooms
// On close / error:
//   1. leaveRoom all current rooms for this peer
//   2. broadcast presence.sync to each affected room

// Helper: broadcastPresence(rooms: string[]) → for each room:
//   broadcast({ type: 'presence.sync', scopeType, scopeId, members: getRoomMembers(room) })
```

Scope/ID extraction from room string:
```ts
// 'chat:<id>' → scopeType: 'chat', scopeId: id
// 'board:<id>' → scopeType: 'board', scopeId: id
function roomToScope(room: string): { scopeType: ScopeType; scopeId: string }
```

The `wrappers` Map in `_ws.ts` already tracks `peerId → RoomPeer`. Extend it to also
carry the ephemeral `PresenceMember` data (received in first subscribe message from client).

Client sends on subscribe:
```json
{ "type": "subscribe", "rooms": ["board:abc"], "member": { "id": "...", "label": "User 1234" } }
```

Add `member?: PresenceMember` to `ClientMessage` interface. Store in wrapper.

## Done when

- [ ] Opening two tabs: each sees the other in `presence.sync` broadcast within 500 ms
- [ ] Closing one tab: other tab receives `presence.sync` with one fewer member
- [ ] `bun run test` — WS handler tests pass (mock peer, mock broadcast)
